	(text "The display used is the Sharp LS013B7DH03\n\nThis display is \"memory in pixel\", meaning that the image on the LCD\ncould be static for long periods of time. To prevent image burning on the LCD\nthe common electrode (COM) needs to be periodically flipped. Flipping the common\nelectrode can be done in 2 different ways:\n1. When you send a SPI command, you can tell the display to flip the COM.\nThis would mean leaving EXTMODE LOW, and sending SPI commands to the display periodically.\n2. You can leave EXTMODE HIGH, and have an MCU hardware timer send a pulse to the \nEXTCOMIN pin to periodically flip it for you.\n\nI'm going with option #2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 183.896 36.322 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4cebac7b-1c04-4211-b0c1-560bf8ebc07f")
	)
